## Why This Is Asked
This question tests extending Boolean logic to 3-valued systems with biconditionals in realistic feature-flag scenarios, plus constraint propagation and backtracking techniques.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic for →, ∧, ∨ operations
- Biconditional as (A→B) ∧ (B→A)
- Constraint propagation with Unknown handling and backtracking
- Feature-flag rollout scenarios with partial information

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene values: F < U < T
const rank = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F': v==='F'?'T':'U'; }
function implies(a,b){ const na = not(a); return [na, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]>=rank[y]?x:y); }
function and(a,b){ return [a, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]<=rank[y]?x:y); }
function or(a,b){ return [a, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]>=rank[y]?x:y); }
```

## Approach
The propagation algorithm iteratively applies constraints, treating U as flexible until forced to T or F. When conflicts arise, it backtracks systematically through the remaining U values.

## Why This Is Asked

Tests design of a constraint solver for non-classical logics with custom operators and propagation strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued semantics (T > U > F)
- Custom operators →* (strong implication) and ⊕ (parity)
- Forward checking, variable ordering, and backtracking in non-deterministic domains

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Kleene 3-valued semantics (T=1, U=0, F=-1)
const T=1, U=0, F=-1;
function not(v){ return v===T?F : v===F?T : U; }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return T; }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ if(a===T||b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F; }
function strongImpl(a,b){ // placeholder behavior for demonstration
  if(a===F) return T; if(a===T) return b; return (b===F?F:(b===U?U:T));
}
function parity(a,b){ // placeholder: U propagates unless forced by T/F
  if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===T&&b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F;
}
```

