## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason with Kleene 3-valued logic in a realistic policy-engine style, including short-circuit semantics and propagation.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic: ¬ flips T/F, U→U; ∧/∨ follow min/max with T>U>F; A→B as ¬A ∨ B.
- Short-circuit evaluation in rule engines.
- Backtracking propagation for constraint satisfaction in a 3-valued setting.

## Code Example
```javascript
function kleeneNot(a){ return a === 'T' ? 'F' : a === 'F' ? 'T' : 'U' }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ /* min/max with T>U>F */ return (a === 'T' || b === 'T') ? 'T' : (a === 'U' || b === 'U') ? 'U' : 'F' }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ return (a === 'F' || b === 'F') ? 'F' : (a === 'U' || b === 'U') ? 'U' : 'T' }
function implies(a,b){ // ¬a ∨ b
  const na = kleeneNot(a)
  return kleeneOr(na, b)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does the answer change if short-circuiting is disabled? 
- How would you extend to detect unsatisfiable sets with more variables?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests reasoning with Kleene 3-valued logic in a constraint set that mirrors feature-flag policies. Requires a lightweight backtracking propagator that respects Unknowns and prevents false violations.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene 3-valued semantics
- Implication under uncertainty
- Lightweight backtracking propagator design
- Constraint satisfaction with Unknowns

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal 3-valued values and a propagation stub
const V = {T:1, F:0, U:2}
function not(x){ return x===V.T?V.F : x===V.F?V.T : V.U }
function or(a,b){ return a===V.T||b===V.T?V.T : (a===V.U||b===V.U?V.U : V.F) }
function and(a,b){ return a===V.F||b===V.F?V.F : (a===V.T && b===V.T ? V.T : V.U) }
function implies(p,q){ const np = not(p); return or(np,q) }
```

